---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Thanks & how it's built · myprettycloud"
  description="Where the 3D assets come from (KayKit by Kay Lousberg, CC0) and a plain-English tour of the technology behind myprettycloud."
>
  <main class="thanks container">
    <header class="thanks__head">
      <p class="thanks__eyebrow">Colophon</p>
      <h1>Built on other people's good work.</h1>
      <p class="thanks__lede">
        myprettycloud is a city you can read, and a city needs a world. Almost everything you see
        in it — every building, cart, mountain and starship — was made by someone else and shared
        freely. This page says where it came from, and how the rest is put together.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="thanks__block" aria-labelledby="assets-title">
      <h2 id="assets-title">The 3D world — KayKit</h2>
      <p>
        Every model in the city comes from <strong>KayKit</strong> by
        <a href="https://kaylousberg.itch.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Kay Lousberg</a
        >. The medieval town is built from the <em>KayKit Medieval Hexagon Pack</em>; the space
        station from <em>KayKit Space Base Bits</em>. Both are released under
        <a
          href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons Zero</a
        > — free to use, even commercially, with no obligation to credit.
      </p>
      <p class="thanks__warm">
        We credit anyway, because this product simply would not look like itself without that kit.
        Thank you, Kay. ♥
      </p>
      <p>
        If you make games or toys, go and get the packs —
        <a href="https://kaylousberg.itch.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >kaylousberg.itch.io</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Self-hosting myprettycloud?</strong> The source code is open (AGPL-3.0), but the
        3D models are not shipped with it. Buy the <em>Source Files</em> edition of the
        <a
          href="https://kaylousberg.itch.io/kaykit-medieval-hexagon"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Medieval Hexagon Pack</a
        > and of
        <a href="https://kaylousberg.itch.io/space-base-bits" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Space Base Bits</a
        >, then run <code>npm run assets:install</code>. The repository's
        <code>docs/ASSETS.md</code> walks you through it step by step.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="thanks__block" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <h2 id="how-title">How the app works, in plain English</h2>
      <p>
        You sign in with your Clever Cloud account. From then on, myprettycloud keeps asking Clever
        Cloud one question on a loop: <em>how is each of your apps and add-ons doing right now?</em>
        Every answer — running or failed, busy or idle, how much memory and disk it's using — is
        painted onto a building. A failed deploy catches fire; a busy service spins its mill faster;
        network traffic fills the roads between buildings.
      </p>
      <p>
        On top of that live picture you can arm <strong>workflows</strong>: rules like <em>“if this
        app's CPU stays above 80% for five minutes, tell my Slack.”</em> When a rule trips, the city
        reacts — a bell tolls, the building smokes — and the notification goes out. That's the whole
        loop: <strong>sign in → watch → react.</strong>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="thanks__block" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
      <h2 id="stack-title">The technology</h2>
      <p>Nothing exotic — just solid, boring pieces doing one job each:</p>
      <dl class="stack">
        <div class="stack__row">
          <dt>The city</dt>
          <dd>
            Renders in your browser with <strong>Three.js</strong> and
            <strong>react-three-fiber</strong>, inside a <strong>Next.js</strong> / React app.
            It's a static site — the 3D models stream in from object storage.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="stack__row">
          <dt>The brain</dt>
          <dd>
            A <strong>Rust</strong> backend (the Axum framework) polls Clever Cloud, evaluates your
            workflow rules and sends notifications. It stores your city layout and rules in
            <strong>PostgreSQL</strong>.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="stack__row">
          <dt>Live updates</dt>
          <dd>
            Changes reach the city over a <strong>WebSocket</strong> the moment they happen —
            sub-second when Clever Cloud's deployment webhooks are wired up, otherwise on a short
            poll.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="stack__row">
          <dt>AI access</dt>
          <dd>
            The backend speaks the <strong>Model Context Protocol</strong>, so an assistant like
            Claude can read your monitors and author workflows for you.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="stack__row">
          <dt>Where it runs</dt>
          <dd>
            Everything is hosted on <strong>Clever Cloud</strong> — backend, the web app, and this
            site — a European, sovereign host. See our <a href="/terms">terms &amp; privacy</a>.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <p class="thanks__back"><a href="/">← Back home</a></p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .thanks {
    max-width: 48rem;
    padding-block: 8rem var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .thanks__head {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .thanks__eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .thanks__head h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: 1.04;
  }

  .thanks__lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-lg);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  .thanks__block {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: var(--rule-hair) solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .thanks__block h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-md);
  }

  .thanks__block p {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-block: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .thanks__block strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .thanks__block a {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
    text-decoration-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-accent-bright) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .thanks__block a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent-bright);
  }

  .thanks__warm {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    color: var(--color-copper) !important;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
  }

  .stack {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .stack__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    padding-block: var(--space-md);
    border-top: var(--rule-hair) solid var(--color-rule-2);
  }

  .stack__row:first-child {
    border-top: none;
  }

  .stack dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
  }

  .stack dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .stack dd strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .stack dd a {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
  }

  .thanks__back {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .thanks__back a {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .thanks__back a:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .thanks {
      padding-block-start: 6.5rem;
    }

    .stack__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-2xs);
    }
  }
</style>
